        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to introduce No. 22 Graydon Crescent to the market, a beautifully presented three-bedroom mid-terrace home ideally situated within the highly regarded Graydon development in Newcastle, County Dublin.\n\nBuilt by Cairn Homes in 2021, this impressive A-rated property extends to approximately 117 sq.m. and offers bright, contemporary and energy-efficient accommodation throughout, making it an ideal choice for modern family living.\n\nThe ground floor features a welcoming entrance hallway, spacious front living room, guest bathroom, separate utility room and a superb open-plan kitchen/dining area overlooking the rear garden. Upstairs, there are three well-proportioned double bedrooms, with the main bedroom benefiting from a stylish ensuite, along with a modern family bathroom.\n\nOutside, the property enjoys a beautifully landscaped west-facing rear garden which offers a private and low-maintenance outdoor space. To the front, there is a private driveway providing valuable off-street parking.\n\nGraydon enjoys an enviable location in the heart of Newcastle Village, with a wide range of amenities close by including schools, shops, parks and leisure facilities. Excellent transport links are also within easy reach, with the N7 and M50 providing convenient access to Dublin City Centre and surrounding areas.\n\nNo. 22 Graydon Crescent is a fantastic opportunity to acquire a turn-key, A-rated family home in a popular and well-established modern development.\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate all this wonderful home has to offer.\n\nDetails\n3 bed, 3 bath\nMid-Terrace\nc.117 sq.m.\nA2 Energy Rating/ Green Mortgage Potential\nAir to water heat pump\nProfessionally landscaped west facing rear garden\nBuilt c.2021\n10 Year Homebond Warranty in place\nDriveway with off-street parking\nQuiet residential development\nClose to local shops, schools & amenities\nEasy access to N7, M50 & surrounding areas\nEarly viewing advised\n\nBER\nBER: A2\n\nDirections\nEircode: D22F6H3"
